hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18987","Waki and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated, from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, Ibn Jafar said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym al-Juhani, he said: The letter of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us while we were in the land of Juhaynah, and I was a young lad: Do not benefit from carrion by skin nor sinew."
"18988","Waki narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from his brother Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: We entered upon Abdullah ibn Ukaym while he was sick, visiting him, and it was said to him: Would you hang something He said: Should I hang something when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever hangs something is entrusted to it."
"18989","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Khalid, from al-Hakam, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wrote to us a month before his death: Do not benefit from carrion by skin nor sinew."
"18990","Khalaf ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Abbad, meaning Ibn Abbad, narrated to us, he said: Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym al-Juhani, he said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us in the land of Juhaynah, he said: and I was a young lad, a month or two before his death: Do not benefit from carrion by skin nor sinew."
"18991","Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Hilal, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came to us, or he said: wrote to us: Do not benefit from carrion by skin nor sinew."
"18992","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Layla narrating from Abdullah ibn Ukaym, that he said: The letter of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was read to us in the land of Juhaynah, and I was a young lad: Do not enjoy from carrion by skin nor sinew."
"18993","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad, meaning Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother Isa, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever hangs something is left to it."
